  "_style": "Write in Tajik Cyrillic (use ғ ӣ қ ӯ ҳ ҷ correctly, never Russian substitutes like г/и/к/у/х/ч). Always address the user informally with “ту” (verbs in 2nd person singular: “Ту метавонӣ…”, possessive -ат/-и ту); address the couple as “шумо ду” / “ҳар дуи шумо” and say “якҷоя” for together, never the formal singular “Шумо”. The other person is always “ёрат” (= ёри ту; “ёр” for the generic noun), never шавҳар/зан/дӯстдухтар/дӯстписар; Tajik has no grammatical gender, so keep sentences neutral and use “ӯ” only when unavoidable, preferably repeating “ёрат” or the name. The partner's name placeholder (%@) is never declined or suffixed: do not attach -ро, izofat -и, or possessive endings to it (not “%@-ро”, “%@и”); rephrase with prepositions or a noun (“ба %@”, “аз %@”, “барои %@”, “%@ мактуб навишт”). Quotes: outer « », inner „ “; ellipsis is one character …; em dash — with spaces; no space before . , : ; ? !; keep emoji, “ · ”, \\n and every placeholder exactly. Numbers: non-breaking space as thousands separator, decimal comma (1 250,5); after a numeral the noun stays singular (“5 рӯз”, “3 дарахт”); dates like “14 ноябри 2026” or 14.11.2026, 24-hour time 21:30. Plural categories: [\"other\"] only — fill “other” with a single form using the singular noun. Buttons and actions are short infinitive or verbal-noun phrases without “лутфан” (“Захира кардан”, “Фиристодан”, “Об додан”); titles, tabs, buttons and headers use sentence case (only the first word capitalized) except proper names like Coupley and Premium. Tone: warm, light and kind, natural Tajik as people speak it in Dushanbe — never cheesy, never word-for-word.",
